            "review_title": "Review at Casinha",
            "review_text": "Joao Duarte\nLisbon, Portugal3 contributions\n1\nThe Finest Ambassador of Portuguese Cuisine in the World!\nMay 2026 • Couples\nI have been traveling all over the globe for nearly 15 years. I have one unshakeable golden rule: whenever there is a Portuguese restaurant in a city, I test it. Needless to say, I have seen my fair share of concepts, reinterpretations, and traditional spots.\nWell, Casinha goes straight to the very top. It is clearly the standard-bearer of Portuguese cuisine just the way we love it—the finest ambassador of Portugal abroad. Finding this level of authenticity and mastery in Ho Chi Minh City is an absolute triumph.\nMy wife and I are currently traveling through Vietnam, and we have just finished our 4th visit to this restaurant in the span of 48 hours (1 breakfast, 1 lunch, and 2 dinners)! That number speaks for itself.\nEvery single dish was a culinary revelation, with some very special mentions for execution that borders on perfection:\n• The Amêijoas (Clams): Quite simply the best we have ever eaten in our lives. The flavor, the cooking, the seasoning... a masterclass.\n• The Bacalhau do Poeta: A dish of fabulous refinement, executed with remarkable technical precision.\n• The Bifana: It is exactly as a bifana should always be. Authentic, flavorful, no fuss—just perfect.\n• The Pastel de Nata: The ultimate must-try. And I weigh my words carefully: it is better than 99.9% of what you can find in Portugal itself.\nWhether it is the accuracy of the flavors, the quality of the ingredients, or the warm atmosphere that instantly reminds you of home, everything is flawless. Casinha makes zero compromises on the authenticity of its gastronomy, and that is what makes it an exceptional dining experience.\nIf you are passing through Saigon and looking for the pinnacle of Portuguese cuisine, look no further. Quite simply a must-visit. A huge thank you to the whole team!\nRead more\nWritten May 17, 2026",
